From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:06:21 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] safetylib: options to keep fewer loop variables relational

With static packing, the variables of every while loop condition, with the
variables they depend on and those that depend on them, are in the
relational domain, whose operations cost far more than those of the
interval domain. With "relational_loop_vars": false, only those of the
functions listed in "relational_loop_vars_in" are, closed over the
variables of the same functions. Fewer relational variables can only add
alarms.

Signed-off-by: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
